  "description": "Denis Yurchak was scrolling Twitter in March when he saw Pieter Levels tweet about Skype shutting down and how big of a loss it would be. Six months later, he runs a $15K MRR with 10,000 users mini-skype. This video breaks down his weekend MVP sprint, how he automated support to stay solo, and why timing a product launch around a billion-dollar company shutdown created instant demand.\n\n🛠️ Want to build your own app with AI? Check out Starter Story Build → https://build.starterstory.com/build/ai-build-accelerator?utm_source=youtube&utm_campaign=denis\n\nDenis' app: https://www.yadaphone.com\nFollow Denis: https://x.com/denisyurchak\n\n🔔 Follow the Second Channel: ‪@StarterStoryBuild‬ \n🏁 We're hiring: starterstory.com/jobs\n\nChapters:\n0:00 - Intro\n0:54 - Who is Denis\n1:13 - Numbers behind Yadaphone\n1:59 - What is Yadaphone\n3:09 - Non-technical background\n4:08 - The $100K tweet\n5:08 - Building the app in a weekend\n6:30 - How to get users overnight\n7:51 - What made Yadaphone successful\n8:39 - Denis' successful app playbook\n11:54 - Tech stack\n12:33 - Do this from Day 1\n13:44 - The final word\n\nThis video is an educational case study of one founder’s experience. It is not financial advice and does not guarantee any income or results. Every business is different and your results may vary.",
